<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Curt von François</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Curt von François was a German army officer and explorer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. As commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">South West Africa</a>, he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/windhoek">Windhoek</a> in 1890 as the colony's military and administrative centre. In 1893 he led an attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hendrik-witbooi">Hendrik Witbooi</a>'s camp at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hornkranz">Hornkranz</a>, in which many women and children were killed, and he was replaced the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/curt-von-francois.jpg" alt="Curt von François" width="320" height="548" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CurtvonFrancois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
